WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.920
A secure Python AI application is more than a Python program that calls a model.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:17.060
It is a system that combines application logic, users, identities, prompts, model responses, data sources, retrieval, tools, APIs, storage, logs, and outputs.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:23.120
Each part can influence what the application sees, what it believes, what it reveals, and what it does.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:28.700
Security work starts by treating the whole system as the product, not just the model endpoint or the prompt string.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:44.360
These applications appear in many forms: chat applications, internal assistants, retrieval augmented generation systems, workflow agents, coding assistants, document analysis tools, customer support helpers, security copilots, and automation services.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.940
Some are interactive.

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.840
Some run in background jobs.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:55.500
Some summarize documents, call tools, draft tickets, search internal knowledge, or help users make decisions.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:02.120
The security stakes depend on the data exposed, the authority granted, and the actions the application can influence.

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:04.180
It helps to separate roles.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.960
A model generates predictions from context.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:11.900
An application decides what context the model receives and what happens with the output.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:14.440
An agent can plan or invoke tools.

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:21.380
A tool performs a bounded capability such as reading a record, creating a ticket, querying a database, or calling an API.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.000
A retrieval system finds supporting content.

00:01:24.220 --> 00:01:27.100
An integration connects the application to another system.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:32.920
Confusing these roles often leads teams to trust model output where application controls should be making the decision.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:36.100
AI application security is not only model safety.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:50.080
Ordinary Python application security still applies: authentication, authorization, input validation, output encoding, secrets management, dependency review, secure logging, testing, monitoring, and incident response.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:57.980
AI-specific risks appear when natural-language input can influence data access, tool calls, workflow decisions, or user beliefs.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:06.200
The secure design goal is useful automation with clear trust boundaries, narrow authority, validated outputs, and observable behavior.
